<PageTitle>AmigoAlert - Emergency Contact Help</PageTitle>

<h1>AmigoAlert: Help for Emergency Contacts</h1>

<p>Bookmark this page to refer back to it at any time.</p>

<h3>What is an emergency contact?</h3>
<p>Amigo Alert lets someone send an alert to the people they trust when they need help. If someone asked you to be their emergency contact, you will be notified when they send an alert.</p>

<h3>How you are added</h3>
<p>You will receive a text message with a consent link. Open the link to review the terms, then choose <strong>Accept</strong> or <strong>Decline</strong>. You are only added as a contact if you accept.</p>

<h3>What you will receive</h3>
<p>After you accept, you will receive text messages when the person who added you sends an alert. If they chose to share it, the message includes their location.</p>

<h3>If you receive an alert</h3>
<p>Try to contact the person right away. If you believe they are in danger, call your local emergency services.</p>

<h3>Stop receiving notifications</h3>
<p>Ask the person who added you to remove you as a contact. If you have not yet responded to a consent link, choose <strong>Decline</strong> and you will not receive notifications.</p>
